            <ArticleTitle>[Introduction of intra-aortic balloon pumping catheter through left subclavian artery guided by trans-esophageal echocardiography].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>411-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is very difficult to insert an intra-aortic balloon pumping catheter into the descending aorta through the subclavian artery by the blind technique. But the technique with the guidance by trans-esophageal echocardiography to introduce the balloon into the descending aorta was simple and useful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
